material: 20 careers walked per arm, 847 matches of mine in arm A and 847 in arm B, 28 Champions League deciders captured (22 second legs), 0 reports whose week did not read as their competition
1) Goals land in the board at a measured share, and the board adds no goals
   arm A: 847 matches, 2398 goals in the ninety and the boards (3 more in extra time): 97 at 45+ (4.05 percent, band 2 to 6), 216 at 90+ (9.01 percent, band 6 to 10)
   goals per match in the ninety and the boards: board open 2.831, board closed 2.831 (847 matches), gap 0.000 (tolerance 0.05)
   of each half's own goals: 8.61 percent of the first half's in its board, 16.99 percent of the second half's; mean boards 3.64 and 6.32 minutes
2) Every line in a board says so, everywhere a minute is printed
   231361 lines read, 18781 of them in a board, each within its board; 598 goals in a board
   report card: 329 board goals printed with their plus on 400 cards; match centre timeline: 598 board goal rows; live commentary: 124 matches equal to their report, 47 board goals with their plus
   changes inside the second half's board: 479 (160 at 90 on the dot, 135 in an eight minute board), each keeping what the clock had reached and filing what it drew inside the board
3) Extra time only on a level knockout tie
   364 deciders read (walk and 12 replays each): 37 level after ninety and the board, 37 with extra time
   819 other matches (league, group, cup, first legs), 152 of them level: none with extra time or a minute past 90
4) The aggregate on a second leg, everywhere the tie is shown
   286 second legs: the tie line, secondLegContext before and after and the match centre's first leg all equal the bracket's first leg plus tonight (21 settled on away goals, 13 in extra time)
   286 report cards print the first leg and the aggregate and where the tie ended; 120 brackets label 748 finished ties' headlines as the aggregate; 44 second legs through the viewer show the aggregate at the interval, at 70 and at the end
   22 first legs carry their own score as the aggregate so far; 400 other weeks have no second leg context and no first leg in the match centre
5) A save from before this round loads and plays
   48 saves stripped of 220 fields from this round, opened with loadCareer and played: 48 matches, 32 with a first half drawn before the round and 16 with both halves, every board rolled in its old range and no old half grew a plus

simCmStoppageTime: PASS. Goals fall in the board at a measured share without adding any, every line in a board says 45+N or 90+N wherever a minute is printed, extra time comes only on a level knockout tie, a second leg shows the first leg and the running aggregate everywhere the tie is shown, and a save from before the round loads and plays.
